  "detailed_answer": "After successfully concluding the North Africa campaign in May 1943, the Allies immediately began planning their next move. In July 1943, they launched Operation Husky - the invasion of Sicily, which was the first major Allied assault on Axis territory in Europe. Following the successful conquest of Sicily, the Allies then invaded mainland Italy in September 1943, beginning the Italian campaign that would continue until the end of World War II in Europe. This strategic movement from North Africa to Sicily and then Italy was a crucial step in opening up a second front against the Axis powers in Europe."
